Speed: CFI on indirect calls, but not on those to the application.

Chrome's PGO profile is recorded from a build with CFI on virtual and
indirect calls; the checks are branches in each function's control flow,
so a function whose checks are missing gets no profile. Indirect calls are
checked against the functions of the LTO unit, and a library calls
functions of the application's: the C API's callbacks, and what an
application gives the libraries the engine exports. Those call sites, and
only those, are left unchecked: a list of zebkit's own, beside Chromium's
tools/cfi/ignores.txt, so that changing it rebuilds only the builds that
check indirect calls.

diff --git a/build/config/sanitizers/BUILD.gn b/build/config/sanitizers/BUILD.gn
index 1354d18e31..2bbf5b4660 100644
--- a/build/config/sanitizers/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/sanitizers/BUILD.gn
@@ -429,7 +429,11 @@ config("cfi_flags") {
     }
 
     if (use_cfi_icall) {
-      cflags += [ "-fsanitize=cfi-icall" ]
+      cflags += [
+        "-fsanitize=cfi-icall",
+        "-fsanitize-ignorelist=" +
+            rebase_path("//tools/cfi/zebkit_icall_ignores.txt", root_build_dir),
+      ]
       # TODO(crbug.com/40266913): Add cflags += [
       # "-fsanitize-cfi-icall-experimental-normalize-integers" ]
       # TODO(crbug.com/40266913): Add rustflags += [
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/cfi/zebkit_icall_ignores.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+#!special-case-list-v2
+
+# zebkit: the calls through function pointers that can reach the
+# application's functions, which CFI does not know (build/config/sanitizers,
+# with use_cfi_icall; ignores.txt is Chromium's and stays as it is).
+#
+# The engine is a library. Its own code calls the application's callbacks,
+# the function pointers of the C API, and the libraries it exports
+# (<zebkit/vendor/*.h>) call the ones an application gives them:
+# allocators, streams, destroy and font functions, comparators. None is in
+# the engine's LTO unit, so a check on such a call would always fail.
+#
+# Chrome's PGO profile is recorded with these checks, and a function whose
+# checks are missing gets no profile: what is listed is as narrow as the
+# library allows. Where an application's function can be called from almost
+# anywhere in a library (an error handler, an allocator, a stream), the
+# library is listed whole, as it was without the checks.
+#
+# base::BindOnce of a function pointer is already left unchecked by
+# Chromium's fun:*FunctorTraits*, std::function's by its libc++ entries.
+
+[cfi-icall]
+
+# The engine's own code: zebkit's C API, its callbacks and hooks.
+src:*zebkit/engine/*
+src:*zebkit/ffmpeg/*
+
+# ICU: common/ is in Chromium's list. In i18n/, a regular expression's
+# callbacks, an application's UCharIterator and UReplaceable, and the
+# opener udat_registerOpener() installs.
+fun:*RegexMatcher*findProgressInterrupt*
+fun:*RegexMatcher*IncrementTime*
+fun:*RuleBasedCollator*compare*UCharIterator*
+fun:udat_open*
+src:*third_party/icu/source/i18n/uitercollationiterator.cpp
+src:*third_party/icu/source/i18n/utrans.cpp
+
+# HarfBuzz: destroy callbacks, an application's font, unicode, draw and
+# paint functions, its table and table-tag functions, buffer messages.
+# Shaping itself (hb-ot-*) keeps its checks.
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-blob.cc
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-blob.hh
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-object.hh
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-draw.cc
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-draw.hh
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-paint.cc
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-paint.hh
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-face.hh
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-font.hh
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-unicode.cc
+src:*third_party/harfbuzz/src/src/hb-unicode.hh
+fun:hb_face_create_for_tables
+fun:hb_face_destroy
+fun:hb_face_set_get_table_tags_func
+fun:hb_face_get_table_tags
+fun:hb_font_destroy
+fun:hb_font_set_funcs
+fun:hb_font_set_funcs_data
+fun:hb_font_funcs_destroy
+fun:hb_font_funcs_set_*_func
+fun:*_hb_font_funcs_set_middle*
+fun:*_hb_font_funcs_set_draw_glyph_func*
+fun:*trampoline*
+fun:*hb_font_draw_glyph_closure_destroy*
+fun:*hb_font_paint_glyph_closure_destroy*
+fun:hb_buffer_set_message_func
+fun:*hb_buffer_t*message_impl*
+
+# FreeType: base/ holds the application's memory, streams, outline
+# functions, finalizers and modules; then a debug hook as the interpreter,
+# and the spans of direct rendering.
+src:*third_party/freetype/src/src/base/*
+src:*third_party/freetype/src/src/gzip/*
+src:*third_party/freetype/src/builds/unix/*
+fun:TT_Run_Context
+fun:gray_sweep_direct
+
+# zlib: an application's zalloc and zfree, and inflateBack's in and out.
+fun:*deflateInit2_
+fun:*deflateEnd
+fun:*deflateCopy
+fun:*inflateInit2_
+fun:*inflateReset2
+fun:*inflateEnd
+fun:*inflateCopy
+fun:updatewindow
+src:*third_party/zlib/infback.c
+
+# Whole libraries, whose application functions are called throughout.
+src:*third_party/zstd/*
+src:*third_party/brotli/*
+src:*third_party/boringssl/*
+src:*third_party/sqlite/*
+src:*third_party/leveldatabase/*
+src:*third_party/libxml/*
+src:*third_party/libwebp/*
+src:*third_party/libjpeg_turbo/*
+src:*third_party/ffmpeg/*
+src:*third_party/dav1d/*
+src:*third_party/opus/*
+src:*third_party/libvpx/*
+src:*third_party/pdfium/*
